  "title": "Lime and coconut chiffon cake",
  "subtitle": "oil-based sponge with whipped egg whites and a coconut milk crumb",
  "excerpt": "Chiffon cake uses oil rather than butter and whipped egg whites folded in at the end to give it a characteristic lightness: tender and moist from the oil, yet airy from the meringue. This version uses coconut milk in place of ordinary milk, with two limes' worth of zest in the batter. The result is a fragrant, very light sponge that bakes in a tube or angel food cake tin, inverted to cool upside down so gravity keeps the crumb open.",
