      "slug": "chiffon-cake",
      "term": "Chiffon cake",
      "definition": "A type of American cake made with vegetable oil rather than solid fat, which keeps it moist when cold. Whipped egg whites are folded into the oil-and-yolk base batter, giving the characteristic light, tender crumb. It must be baked in an ungreased tube tin and inverted to cool."
