            "text": "chiffon cake"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " tin must not be greased: the batter needs to climb the sides of the tube pan as it rises, and a greased tin causes the cake to slide down and collapse. Buy a dedicated tube pan with a removable base if you make chiffon cakes regularly. The cake is inverted to cool, resting upside down on its tube legs or balanced on a bottle neck over the counter, so gravity does the work of maintaining the open crumb as it sets."
          }
        ]
      },
