      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Make the batter"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Heat the oven to 165°C (conventional). Do not grease the tube tin. Sift {{plain-flour}}, 150 g {{caster-sugar}}, {{baking-powder}}, and {{sea-salt-fine}} into a large bowl. Make a well in the centre. Add {{vegetable-oil}}, {{egg-yolks}}, {{coconut-milk}}, the zest from both limes (substituting {{lemon}} slug for lime), and {{lemon-juice}} (lime juice). Whisk vigorously until the batter is completely smooth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Whip and fold the meringue"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In a clean, grease-free bowl, whisk {{egg-whites}} with {{cream-of-tartar}} until foamy. Gradually add the remaining 50 g {{caster-sugar}}, whisking until stiff, glossy peaks form. The meringue should hold a firm peak but not look dry or grainy. Fold one-third of the meringue into the batter with a large spatula to lighten it, then fold in the remaining two-thirds in two additions, working gently to keep as much air as possible."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 3
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Bake and invert"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pour the batter into the ungreased tube tin and smooth the top. Bake for 50 to 55 minutes until the top is golden and springs back firmly when pressed, and a skewer comes out clean. Immediately invert the tin onto its legs or onto a bottle neck to cool completely, about 1 hour 30 minutes. Do not remove the cake from the tin until fully cool; removing it warm causes the delicate crumb to tear. To unmould, run a thin knife around the outer and inner edges of the tin, then press out through the removable base."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
